        "referee": "Stuart Attwell",
        "standfirst": "Everton recovered from a goal down to beat Coventry City 3-1.",
        "account": "Yann Gboho put Coventry City ahead in the 52nd minute with a low right-footed shot from inside the box that went in at the corner. Everton were level four minutes after Gboho's goal, when Vitalii Mykolenko crossed and Thierno Barry headed the ball into the top corner of the Coventry net from within the box. Barry gave Everton the lead after 61 minutes, drilling a left-footed finish from close range into the bottom corner. With nine minutes left, Barry played a through ball to Kiernan Dewsbury-Hall, whose low left-footed shot from a tight angle found the corner.",
        "sections": [
          {
            "head": "Barry double, Mykolenko assist",
            "pitch": "Thierno Barry had six shots, and his pair took him to six league goals for the campaign, alongside the pass that set up Dewsbury-Hall. Vitalii Mykolenko earned a defensive point to go with the cross for the leveller.",
